\subsection[Class imbalance and federation]{\rev{Class imbalance and federation}}

\rev{Under the 9:1 SR:AF class imbalance the hand-crafted features overtook ECGFounder. At this natural-like ratio (majority 0.90) the ARI of every representation above chance level fell. A 10\% minority class gives a clusterer fewer records from which to form a cluster of its own. That may explain part of the fall, and we did not test it. The hand-crafted features retained the most structure over the ten seeds (ARI 0.265 [0.250, 0.280], AMI 0.245 [0.233, 0.257]), against ARI 0.063 [0.061, 0.065] and AMI 0.148 [0.143, 0.152] for ECGFounder, with no overlap between the two ARI intervals. HuBERT-ECG reached an ARI similar to that of ECGFounder (0.061 [0.053, 0.069]) at a lower AMI (0.044 [0.037, 0.050]). By ARI its partition agreed with the classes on record pairs beyond chance and about as well as that of ECGFounder, and by AMI it carried less information about them. Raw flattening and the conv-AE stayed at chance level (0.000 and 0.004). The reversal was observed at this one ratio and under power scaling, and it is a result for that setting.}

\rev{Non-IID site heterogeneity reduced the ARI of each representation whose centralized ARI is above zero, and it did so unequally. Under IID federation across ten sites every representation retained essentially its centralized ARI, which validates the federated procedure (Table~\ref{tab:fed} and Fig.~\ref{fig:fed}). Under non-IID federation the hand-crafted features retained 92\% of their centralized ARI (0.644 to 0.591), while the ARI of ECGFounder fell from 0.885 to 0.612. The two means were close, 0.612 against 0.591, and they did not carry the same risk. Across the ten redrawn site partitions the seed bootstrap interval of the hand-crafted features was [0.546, 0.631] and their worst single partition still returned 0.455. The interval of ECGFounder was [0.382, 0.796], and three of its ten partitions fell to 0.132 or below, one of them to chance. This study takes the worst site draw as its deployment criterion, because a deployment meets a single site partition, and the mean over ten draws does not show how low that partition can fall. On that criterion the hand-crafted features retained more of their clustering ARI than ECGFounder under simulated site heterogeneity on PTB-XL.}

