\subsection{Deployment cost}

\rev{Of the five representations, ECGFounder, which clustered best, took the longest to compute per record (Table~\ref{tab:cost}). Its extraction took fifteen times as long as the hand-crafted extraction. Both foundation models needed a gigabyte or more of resident memory against \mbox{364\,MB} for the hand-crafted features, about a third of the memory of ECGFounder. The hand-crafted features also carry no learned parameters. Clustering itself was negligible everywhere, under \mbox{0.3\,s} for the whole cohort at any of the five dimensionalities, so the cost of a representation is the cost of extracting it.}

